WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.550
Check yourself with two questions
from the module's knowledge check.

2
00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:06.712
First: Module 4's mover
review is still open,

3
00:00:06.712 --> 00:00:09.513
so there's no transfer-to-review value.

4
00:00:09.513 --> 00:00:11.000
How does the run report it?

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.438
The answer is c: as not measured,
rule L D eight, never as zero.

6
00:00:16.438 --> 00:00:20.438
A zero would look like the best
possible result, and it would be false.

7
00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:23.681
Second: the period
reports zero chain breaks

8
00:00:23.681 --> 00:00:26.925
and zero coverage gaps,
but complete is false.

9
00:00:26.925 --> 00:00:27.613
Why?

10
00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:28.653
The answer is a.

11
00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:34.201
Drift is still open and metrics are out of
bounds, so Gate 7's criteria aren't met.

12
00:00:34.201 --> 00:00:36.261
The period scores the criteria,

13
00:00:36.261 --> 00:00:39.987
and an unbroken chain meets
only the evidence criterion.

14
00:00:39.987 --> 00:00:42.420
The module page has three more questions,

15
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.980
each linked to the
section that teaches it.
